# atomic sandbox replay v1
# M4 "Pin": the Place tool puts a third H on the default camera's focus plane 3.000 Bohr from H2's
# nucleus 0 (at (3.0260, -0.1455, -2.0059) Bohr), then nuclei 0 and 2 are pinned. After the run
# plays and pauses they are still 3 Bohr apart, while nucleus 1 has moved away from R = 1.6 (H2
# starts compressed and vibrates). The pause lands a machine-dependent number of steps after the
# 8 waited for (one DFT step per tick; the Pause arrives while one is solving), hence the range.
view 1400 900
action smooth-motion false
# pinned at the merge of main (2026-10-14): written for the presets' own 49^3 x 0.25 grid (Balanced)
# without container walls, before the app defaulted to Accurate (81^3) with walls on; H2 is the
# R = 1.6 Bohr scene it was written for (h2_r16.scene; the h2 preset is 1.45 Bohr now)
action ionic none
action quality balanced
action walls off 4.5
scene h2_r16.scene
wait idle
action tool place
action element 1
t 100 cursor 0.5560566 0.0237261
t 110 button left down
t 170 button left up
wait idle
expect nuclei 3
expect dist 0 2 2.99 3.01
action pin 0 true
action pin 2 true
action play
wait steps 8
action pause
wait idle
expect paused true
expect dist 0 2 2.99 3.01
expect dist 0 1 1.62 2.2
expect no-error
